{
  "wireMagic": "pb3",
  "pens": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wsWinStyles": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wpWinPositions": [ {
  
  } ],
  "events": [ {
    "tStartMs": 780,
    "dDurationMs": 500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "[Click]"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1340,
    "dDurationMs": 1040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "[High-pitched CRT TV noise]"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2560,
    "dDurationMs": 2760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Film is a very straightforward technology."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 5320,
    "dDurationMs": 2880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It just involves taking a two-dimensional image,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 8200,
    "dDurationMs": 4320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and focusing it on to a two-dimensional piece of film, and there you have a photo."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 12520,
    "dDurationMs": 4160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But video, and by that, I mean moving electronic images,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 16680,
    "dDurationMs": 5600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "has a very different history with a lot of changes that have really transformed the way it works."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 22280,
    "dDurationMs": 2760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This video was sponsored by B\u0026H Photo,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 25040,
    "dDurationMs": 4080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "which is kind of fitting because that's where I get a lot of my gear to make these videos."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 29120,
    "dDurationMs": 4120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So I'll tell you more about them later,\nbut now it's off to San Francisco."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 38080,
    "dDurationMs": 5160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I'm going to meet with a guy who knows a lot about old video gear and he's got some he's gonna show me."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 44080,
    "dDurationMs": 1600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- Richard, nice to meet you."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 45680,
    "dDurationMs": 3920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- Nice to meet you Derek. Come on in. Welcome to LabGuy's World."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 49620,
    "dDurationMs": 2720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- [Laughs.] That's a cool spot you got here."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 52360,
    "dDurationMs": 960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- Thank you."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 53320,
    "dDurationMs": 4920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- The fundamental problem of video is taking this two-dimensional light image"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 58240,
    "dDurationMs": 3720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and turning it into a one-dimensional electrical signal."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 61960,
    "dDurationMs": 2120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So how do you do that?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 64080,
    "dDurationMs": 4440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Well, the solution actually comes from\nthe first ever fax machine,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 68520,
    "dDurationMs": 4640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "which believe it or not,\nwas invented in 1843 by Alexander Bain."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 73160,
    "dDurationMs": 2200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now he was a clock maker."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 75360,
    "dDurationMs": 5160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "His invention involved a transmitter and\nreceiver which each had a pendulum,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 80520,
    "dDurationMs": 2400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and those pendulums were synchronized."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 82920,
    "dDurationMs": 4520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So what would happen is,\nat the transmitter, there would be a metal sheet"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 87440,
    "dDurationMs": 4560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "on which something was written or drawn\nusing a non-conducting ink."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 92000,
    "dDurationMs": 2520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- So a finger at the transmitter,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 94520,
    "dDurationMs": 4600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "an electric finger, would stroke over the paper and wherever there was iron, it would conduct,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 99120,
    "dDurationMs": 2920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and that conducting signal was sent to the other end,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 102040,
    "dDurationMs": 5120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "which was applied to paper with a chemical\nthat would turn dark when electricity flowed through it,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 107160,
    "dDurationMs": 5080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and it would reproduce a very accurate image\nof the handwritten note you just made."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 112240,
    "dDurationMs": 3960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- Now Alexander Bain\nonly ever transmitted static images,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 116200,
    "dDurationMs": 4360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but some people have called him\nthe real father of television,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 120560,
    "dDurationMs": 1560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "because he invented scanning."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 122120,
    "dDurationMs": 3880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This idea of moving back and forth across an image,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 126000,
    "dDurationMs": 2800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "breaking it down into lines."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 128800,
    "dDurationMs": 2680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But if you really want to get moving images,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 131480,
    "dDurationMs": 2640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "well, you need to be able to scan much faster."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 134120,
    "dDurationMs": 7280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So we have to jump forward to 1884, and a 23-year-old German University student named Paul Nipkow."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 141400,
    "dDurationMs": 3200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "He patented what is called the Nipkow disk,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 144600,
    "dDurationMs": 4160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "which is basically a big disc with a spiral of holes in it."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 148760,
    "dDurationMs": 2320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- The inner pinholes do the scanning,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 151080,
    "dDurationMs": 3200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and if I go fast enough you can see the scanning."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 154280,
    "dDurationMs": 2760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- You would put a light behind this Nipkow disk"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 157040,
    "dDurationMs": 5360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and so you'd have a spot of light\nwhich scans across your subject, say a person."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 162400,
    "dDurationMs": 5960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And then there would be a reflected light off that person\nwhich would be picked up by some light sensors."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 168360,
    "dDurationMs": 5120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "That would create an electrical signal which\nyou could transmit over distance to a receiver."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 173480,
    "dDurationMs": 6000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now at the receiver you use that electrical signal\nto modulate the brightness of a light source,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 179480,
    "dDurationMs": 3160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and then in front of that you place\na synchronized Nipkow disk,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 182640,
    "dDurationMs": 4280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and so the result is a recreation\nof the image from the transmitter."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 186920,
    "dDurationMs": 5600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- So it was just barely at the limits\nof the ability to make a viewable picture,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 192520,
    "dDurationMs": 3360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and it was actually broadcast\nfor a couple of years in Britain,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 195880,
    "dDurationMs": 4800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and in America and other countries did\nexperimental broadcasts using this technique."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 200680,
    "dDurationMs": 4320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- This is arguably the first-ever\nbroadcast television image."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 205000,
    "dDurationMs": 3360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It was broadcast for a few hours a day for several years,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 208360,
    "dDurationMs": 4960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and it was used by engineers to perform experiments\nand try to improve the quality of the broadcast."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 213320,
    "dDurationMs": 4160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- What it proved was that this wasn't the way to do it.\n[Laughs.]"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 217480,
    "dDurationMs": 4800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- So by 1939 mechanical TV was all but phased out,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 222280,
    "dDurationMs": 3760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and it was replaced by all-electric TV."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 226160,
    "dDurationMs": 2380,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "♫"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 228600,
    "dDurationMs": 2760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Specifically the cathode-ray tube."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 231360,
    "dDurationMs": 4920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So this is a glass vacuum tube\nwith an electron gun at the back."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 236280,
    "dDurationMs": 3600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And the electron gun would fire\na beam of electrons at the screen,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 239880,
    "dDurationMs": 6280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "where it was coated in a chemical which produced light when it got hit by the electrons that's called a phosphor."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 246160,
    "dDurationMs": 3960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And using magnetic fields, this beam\nwas scanned across the screen"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 250120,
    "dDurationMs": 1680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "top-to-bottom, left-to-right,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 251800,
    "dDurationMs": 5480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and you would vary the brightness of the beam by varying the voltage on a control electrode,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 257280,
    "dDurationMs": 5960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "essentially determining how many electrons would get sent out in that beam at any instant to hit the screen."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 263240,
    "dDurationMs": 2360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So, if you send out a lot of electrons you get a bright spot,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 265650,
    "dDurationMs": 2390,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "if you don't then you get a dark spot,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 268040,
    "dDurationMs": 2960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and in that way you can produce a nice black-and-white image."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 271000,
    "dDurationMs": 2000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And if you're wondering about color TV,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 273000,
    "dDurationMs": 2560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "well, there were a number of dead ends along the path"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 275560,
    "dDurationMs": 3240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to the red-green-blue pixel system\nthat became the standard."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 278800,
    "dDurationMs": 2800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Like this TV with a spinning color wheel."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 281600,
    "dDurationMs": 4120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- I named the project Goldmark I\nin honor of Dr. Goldmark."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 285720,
    "dDurationMs": 4080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The television part is a standard\nblack-and-white picture tube."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 289800,
    "dDurationMs": 6880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- It displayed 24 frames per second but each frame required six scans: blue-green-red, blue-green-red."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 296680,
    "dDurationMs": 5000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It worked really well, but it wasn't backwards compatible with black-and-white TVs."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 302400,
    "dDurationMs": 2040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And this is a mini triniscope,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 304440,
    "dDurationMs": 4280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "so named for its three cathode ray tubes, one for each color."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 308720,
    "dDurationMs": 2680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And their images were combined with prisms."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 311400,
    "dDurationMs": 2360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- The downside of a triniscope monitor"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 313760,
    "dDurationMs": 4280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "is that for every inch you add diagonally to your screen"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 318040,
    "dDurationMs": 5240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the volume of the cabinet increases by like the power of something like three and a half."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 323280,
    "dDurationMs": 2640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "They get huge fast."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 325920,
    "dDurationMs": 4200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- So the ultimate solution was to have red, green, and blue phosphors for each pixel,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 330120,
    "dDurationMs": 3040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and three electron guns to determine their relative brightness."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 333960,
    "dDurationMs": 5240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- Now, the number of lines those electron beams make across the screen is, in theory,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 339200,
    "dDurationMs": 3440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "525 every thirtieth of a second."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 342640,
    "dDurationMs": 5080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But this is achieved by scanning every other line each sixtieth of a second,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 347720,
    "dDurationMs": 3160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "so it actually takes two scans to make one frame."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 350880,
    "dDurationMs": 2440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This is called interlacing."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 353320,
    "dDurationMs": 5320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And what you'll notice watching this is that most of the time you're actually staring at a blank screen."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 358640,
    "dDurationMs": 5320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The illusion of a continuous moving image is made possible by our persistence of vision,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 363960,
    "dDurationMs": 5280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that is, we don't stop seeing something instantaneously after light stops entering our eyes."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 369240,
    "dDurationMs": 2840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- So, initially I was thinking\nthis wouldn't be too hard to film"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 372080,
    "dDurationMs": 5120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I mean, a thirtieth of a second\nor a sixtieth of a second, that's not terribly fast."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 377200,
    "dDurationMs": 6760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But then if you think about it, 262 and 1/2 lines being drawn every sixtieth of a second,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 383960,
    "dDurationMs": 7960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that is 15,750 lines drawn per second."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 393080,
    "dDurationMs": 920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "That is fast,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 394000,
    "dDurationMs": 2880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "so if you want to be able to see the lines being drawn on,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 396880,
    "dDurationMs": 3440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "you need to shoot faster than 15,000 frames per second,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 400320,
    "dDurationMs": 2840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "a lot faster, really, to be able to see this clearly."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 403160,
    "dDurationMs": 6100,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and so I am using the Phantom v2512."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 410000,
    "dDurationMs": 1880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "That is the beast"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 411880,
    "dDurationMs": 2320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that is allowing me to produce these images."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 414200,
    "dDurationMs": 4720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now the actual resolution of these TVs turned out to be around 480 lines,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 418920,
    "dDurationMs": 5480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "so when you select 480p on YouTube,\nthat's why this is an option."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 424400,
    "dDurationMs": 3640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And I guess it's worth pointing out that the \"tube\" in \"YouTube\""
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 428040,
    "dDurationMs": 3080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "is this thing, a cathode-ray tube."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 431120,
    "dDurationMs": 4600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So in the time before light-sensitive chips like we all use in our cameras today,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 435720,
    "dDurationMs": 4160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "how did you actually create the image to display on a television?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 439880,
    "dDurationMs": 2680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Well, there were many vacuum tube designs."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 442560,
    "dDurationMs": 3120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "One of the most common was the image orthicon tube,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 445680,
    "dDurationMs": 1760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "sometimes called Emmy for short."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 447440,
    "dDurationMs": 3200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In fact, that's where the name Emmys comes from."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 450640,
    "dDurationMs": 3920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So the way it would work is you use the camera lens to focus an image"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 454560,
    "dDurationMs": 5600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "onto the front of the image orthicon tube, and that was coated with a photoelectric substance,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 460160,
    "dDurationMs": 3600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "so it would release electrons in proportion to the light that hit them."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 463760,
    "dDurationMs": 3800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now those electrons were collimated by magnetic fields and sent straight back."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 467560,
    "dDurationMs": 4800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So essentially you had an electron version of the image sent straight back to a target,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 472360,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "which was a very, very thin glass plate."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 475360,
    "dDurationMs": 5160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And of course where there's more electrons,\nthat creates a more negative spot on this target."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 480520,
    "dDurationMs": 5520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "From the back of the tube you'd send forward an electron beam to scan across the target."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 486040,
    "dDurationMs": 2160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And so these electrons as they came in,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 488200,
    "dDurationMs": 5240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the more negative a spot that was on the target, the more that beam would get reflected."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 493440,
    "dDurationMs": 3480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And so that reflected beam was amplified in the tube,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 496920,
    "dDurationMs": 6400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and then used as the signal to essentially determine how bright that part of the image should be."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 503320,
    "dDurationMs": 5640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So this is how television images were created and displayed for decades."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 508960,
    "dDurationMs": 2200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But here is the crazy thing:"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 511160,
    "dDurationMs": 3520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "there was no way to record them."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 515640,
    "dDurationMs": 3680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I mean the purpose of video\nor the purpose of electronic images"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 519320,
    "dDurationMs": 4040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "was really to transmit something\nfrom one place to another."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 523360,
    "dDurationMs": 3320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "\"Television\" literally means \"seeing at a distance.\""
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 527160,
    "dDurationMs": 4520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It's not about recording for replaying later as film was."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 531680,
    "dDurationMs": 2280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- The thing that blew me away was"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 533960,
    "dDurationMs": 6280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "realizing that video cameras existed for a couple decades before video tape."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 540240,
    "dDurationMs": 4920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- That's right. That was the the era of live broadcasting"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 545160,
    "dDurationMs": 2080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- But this introduced some problems."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 547240,
    "dDurationMs": 5320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "For example in North America, in the US, a lot of the TV programs were produced out in New York,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 552560,
    "dDurationMs": 3840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and there was a coaxial cable which went across the whole of the US,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 556400,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and that could deliver programming to, say, Los Angeles."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 559400,
    "dDurationMs": 2280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But it was at the wrong time."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 561680,
    "dDurationMs": 3320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I mean a news broadcast from New York at 6:00 or 7:00 p.m."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 565000,
    "dDurationMs": 3680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "couldn't just be broadcast live at 3:00 or 4:00 p.m. on the West Coast."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 568680,
    "dDurationMs": 1360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It just didn't make any sense,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 570040,
    "dDurationMs": 1600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So you needed to time-delay it."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 571640,
    "dDurationMs": 1960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So how did they do it?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 573600,
    "dDurationMs": 3160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Well the answer was to take a film camera,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 576760,
    "dDurationMs": 3640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "a cinema camera, and point it at a television screen,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 580400,
    "dDurationMs": 2800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and actually film the television screen."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 583200,
    "dDurationMs": 2440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Then you would quickly develop the film"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 585640,
    "dDurationMs": 3240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and bring it back three hours later to broadcast it live,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 588880,
    "dDurationMs": 3760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to scan it in and broadcast\nthat film as though it were live."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 592640,
    "dDurationMs": 4160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- But now when I bring it back to the TV studio and stick it into the telecine,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 597640,
    "dDurationMs": 660,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "[Laughs.]"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 598640,
    "dDurationMs": 3600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the picture doesn't look right."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 602240,
    "dDurationMs": 2040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The lines aren't lining up right,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 604280,
    "dDurationMs": 4280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and besides you're trying to sample\ntwo sets of lines back together and they don't!"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 608560,
    "dDurationMs": 4760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- This became such a prevalent method of doing business for the TV networks"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 613320,
    "dDurationMs": 4520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that by 1954 the television networks,\nto time-delay their programming,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 617840,
    "dDurationMs": 5320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "were using more film than all the film studios in Hollywood combined."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 623160,
    "dDurationMs": 3840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This is absurd and expensive and wasteful,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 627000,
    "dDurationMs": 2840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "so a different method was really needed."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 629840,
    "dDurationMs": 6960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And that came along in 1956 with the invention of the first workable video tape recorder."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 636800,
    "dDurationMs": 4800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It was the size of a large desk and it cost a fortune."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 641600,
    "dDurationMs": 6720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It ran on this two-inch magnetic tape with little video heads spinning at 14,000 RPM."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 648320,
    "dDurationMs": 2960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "We're talking as fast as a jet engine."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 651280,
    "dDurationMs": 7020,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "That is the kind of technology it took before\nvideo became what we kind of know it as today,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 658420,
    "dDurationMs": 2320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "a method of recording and storing images,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 660800,
    "dDurationMs": 4880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "rather than a way of just transmitting vision from one place to another."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 665680,
    "dDurationMs": 1920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But we've come a long way since then,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 667600,
    "dDurationMs": 3280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "miniaturizing the tape stand into VHS and Beta,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 670880,
    "dDurationMs": 6320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and eventually down to DV and mini DV,\nand now we are on to solid state storage."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 677200,
    "dDurationMs": 3400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And you know I've glossed over a lot of the history here,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 680600,
    "dDurationMs": 5560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but now we're in a situation\nwhere video is better than film."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 686160,
    "dDurationMs": 4560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "You can see that in 2012,\nthat was the inflection point between"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 690720,
    "dDurationMs": 5200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "people using film to shoot the top-grossing movies,\nchanging over to people using digital."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 696640,
    "dDurationMs": 3480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And what this has done for people like you and me,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 700120,
    "dDurationMs": 4460,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "is it's made it possible to make really good images.\n[Music]"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 704580,
    "dDurationMs": 4220,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And the question I have is,\nwhat does this do to a society?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 708800,
    "dDurationMs": 3980,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "What might it do when people can share\nevery part of their lives with video?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 713920,
    "dDurationMs": 2160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "♫"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 719480,
    "dDurationMs": 5360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This part of this video was sponsored by B\u0026H Photo, literally one of my favorite stores in the world."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 724840,
    "dDurationMs": 5440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "They have all the greatest and newest camera gear, plus pro audio and lighting and computers,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 730280,
    "dDurationMs": 3880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "basically anything you could need to make high-quality video."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 734160,
    "dDurationMs": 3160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And every time I'm out in New York,\nI go and visit the store."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 737320,
    "dDurationMs": 2280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The last time I was there I asked them for a gimbal,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 739600,
    "dDurationMs": 3440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "because I've been seeing all these comments saying my videos were too shaky,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 743040,
    "dDurationMs": 3200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and so they recommend that this one right here,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 746240,
    "dDurationMs": 4240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and I've really loved it. It's so smooth.\nI can hold it with one hand."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 750480,
    "dDurationMs": 5760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It is pretty lightweight and it's just been great\nand I think it's really improved the quality of my videos."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 756240,
    "dDurationMs": 2720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And when I'm back here in LA,\nI still shop with them online,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 758960,
    "dDurationMs": 2880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "because there is no shop like that in LA."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 761840,
    "dDurationMs": 4120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In fact, this camera, the Sony a7R III,\nI'd highly recommend it,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 765960,
    "dDurationMs": 2840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I bought it for my wife for Christmas\nthe Christmas before last,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 768800,
    "dDurationMs": 5470,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and it was backordered, but you can actually sign up through their website to get notified when it's in stock,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 774270,
    "dDurationMs": 2410,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and I did that and managed to get it\nin time for Christmas,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 776680,
    "dDurationMs": 2160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "so it's a really great shopping experience."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 778840,
    "dDurationMs": 4200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The people are so knowledgeable, it's a mom-and-pop shop, it's got anything you could ever want."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 783040,
    "dDurationMs": 4240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I highly recommend that you check out B\u0026H Photo.\nI'll put a link to them in the description."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 787280,
    "dDurationMs": 2220,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And thanks to B\u0026H for sponsoring this video."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 789620,
    "dDurationMs": 1220,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "♫"
    } ]
  } ]
}
